                <pb facs="0234" n="226" sameAs="frus:frus1938v01/pg226"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.00/8215: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Phillips</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-07-07T19:00:00+01:00">July 7, 1938—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received July 7—4 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>169. My telegram 160, June 29, noon. The British Ambassador informs me he has
                    received a telegram from his Government stating that since his representations
                    to Ciano on June 28 there have been no attacks whatsoever on British ships by
                    Franco’s forces.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
